  "requiredSemanticLaws": {
    "V14-L1": "MTS has one ontological primitive Link and one abstract Link-forming operation; the recursive 8/9/6/1 alphabet is the emergent four-way self-incidence classification of that one operation, not four primitive opcodes and not the Anum/Q alphabet. Before a Context frame, the two one-sided cases form an unnamed J-chiral pair; after local orientation they receive START_K/END_K roles.",
    "V14-L2": "Ostensive ∞/♂/♀/⟼ denote ROOT/START/END/PAIR through an explicit grammar.",
    "V14-L3": "Q14 [ ] T F is version-separated from immutable legacy Q13 [ ] 1 0.",
    "V14-L4": "Successful empty reaction {}, active identity, START continuation and END continuation are distinct results.",
    "V14-L5": "Semantic Link identity is immutable; rewrite changes membership/structure rather than poles in place.",
    "V14-L6": "Nat starts at U and uses uniform successor N⟼L; Degree remains a separate scale starting at L.",
    "V14-L7": "Count over canonical ExactSequence returns Nat cardinality.",
    "V14-L8": "Canonical Add is constructor-scoped and is total/function-like over selected Nat evidence.",
    "V14-L9": "Derived Le requires canonical Add proof authority.",
    "V14-L10": "Multiplication/full semiring is explicitly outside the v0.14 acceptance scope.",
    "V14-L11": "Generalized modus ponens/reaction is preserved from accepted v0.13 through the explicit A14 -> A16 -> A17 -> A72w witness chain covering 1->0, 1->1, 1->N, N->1 and N->M without host function/cardinality opcodes.",
    "V14-L12": "A4': before orientation, Link pole positions carry objective global Z2 chirality with no primitive absolute START/END. A Context K is locally oriented by choosing one of its two Link-native one-sided self-incidence markers; this choice determines χ(K) in the objective orbit {W,J(W)} by a J-invariant relative-chirality relation, derives START_K/END_K, and induces relative transport g_AB∈{Id,J} with g_AA=Id, g_AB=g_BA and g_AB∘g_BC=g_AC. No Foundation-global selected W, ExactSequence carrier, host witness argument, or raw Link presence is orientation authority.",
    "V14-L13": "Anum is a rooted compact representation/coding of a sequence of Links; ExactSequence preserves exact positional sequence identity distinct from fold denotation, the recursive Link codec is not Anum, Q is a versioned sequence codec/interpreter, and every local sequence origin is R.",
    "V14-L14": "MTS representation layers are explicit and non-ontological above Link: recursive alphabet, representations/codecs, byte-text and symbolic metanotation introduce no second ontology entity."
